From f37bfb09c420ed1865406db5d28ed1c879fcf5a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manish KL <manishklach@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 05:25:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] mm: hbf: add CXL memory-node backend and LLM KV-cache
 monitor

- hbf_cxl.c: new CXL backend that identifies memory-only NUMA nodes
  (nodes with N_MEMORY but no N_CPU) as CXL-attached memory and
  handles page migration to/from them using the same folio-based
  migration pipeline as the NUMA backend
- Debugfs: /sys/kernel/debug/hbf/cxl/nodes shows detected CXL nodes
  with their memory sizes
- Registration order: CXL backend registered before NUMA backend so
  it takes priority for CXL nodes; NUMA backend handles everything else
- hbfctl: add cxl command to display CXL node info from debugfs
- tools/hbftrace/kvcache_monitor.py: Python monitor that watches
  /proc/PID/numa_maps for pages on suboptimal NUMA nodes and submits
  HBF promote hints; supports vLLM/llama.cpp KV-cache monitoring
- Export hbf_debugfs_root via hbf_get_debugfs_root() accessor
